{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1027642-vtm-mta-crossovers-and-awareness","id":1027642,"title":"VtM/MtA Crossovers And Awareness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-06T07:40:41-08:00","id":1027642,"title":"VtM/MtA Crossovers And Awareness","content":"Would a Mage be able to perceive Auspex's Clairvoyance being used on her with Awareness Talent? E.g.: A Vampire is looking into a room where the Mage is having a conversation with someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10423-rudy23","name":"Rudy23","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:49:51-08:00","id":1027649,"title":"","content":"If a mage can use Awareness to be aware of when a Sorcerer uses one of their paths, then that would probably work for other kinds of supernatural magic.<br /> <br /> For this specific ability, I'm guessing they'd need at least Corr. 1 to be able to sense when someone's peeking on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:10:36-08:00","id":1027669,"title":"","content":"Well, Awareness can detect that some magic it's in use, Auspex it's no exeption. It can't detect the &quot;type&quot; of magic, however (you can &quot;feel a disturbance in the force&quot;, not that that Auspex it's being used to spy you). To detect that, you would need Correspondence 1, perhaps Prime 1 can give some hints too.<br /> Also, usually, the use of Awareness needs to be declared. This depends on the Storyteller, but I think that a Clairvoyance would be subtle enough to pass under the radar, unless the mage has some reason to think it's being scryed (or it's just very paranoid) and decides to &quot;check&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T12:37:41-08:00","id":1027803,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking. Awareness is &quot;You can feel a disturbance in the force.&quot; and higher ranks determine how far you can sense things from. At 5 anyone using magic in the city can potentially ping your radar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T20:00:02-08:00","id":1027994,"title":"","content":"Which could be annoying if there is a healthy population of Sorcerers in the area. I tend to run each type of gifted mortals (Chi Mystics, Faith Mystics, Mythic Sorcerers, Psychic Sorcerers, and Scientific Sorcerers) at a ratio of 1:2,500, so characters with Awareness 5 would be pinged every minute of every hour. Of course, the vast majority (80%) of gifted mortals in my games only have one level in their particular gift, so I would think that minor forms of magic of that sort would be unnoticeable even if you had Awareness 5 unless you were within a city block.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T03:02:39-08:00","id":1028087,"title":"","content":"It is like at the beginning of the year:<br /> You don't hear every explosion, some stand out, but the others form a background of sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T17:25:20-08:00","id":1028344,"title":"","content":"Exactly. I think that the problem that Mage characters face in crossovers is that they are potentially dealing with a relatively large number of entities with hundreds to thousands of years more experience than they possess. In addition, beginning Kindred can shred beginning Mages without that much difficulty in a fair fight, so Mage should endeavor to never fight fair. They should make sure to hunt Kindred at noon and to trap every entrance to their dwelling during the night, either magical or mundane, and they might survive. Or they could make a deal and have reasonably powerful new friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T09:17:00-08:00","id":1028578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1027642-vtm-mta-crossovers-and-awareness?p=1027669#post1027669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To detect that, you would need Correspondence 1, perhaps Prime 1 can give some hints too.<br /> Also, usually, the use of Awareness needs to be declared.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there somewhere where this is specifically stated? <br /> <br /> Based on the description of Awareness (and Alertness) and of Perception in the core book, they can be used actively or reflexively. &quot;I have a bad feeling about this&quot; of &quot;I sense a disturbance in the Force&quot; both imply reflexive use, in fact. (And those are used as examples of 1 dot...) In neither case were the characters in question consciously and actively examining and analyzing the situation or the state of the Force. The situation just pinged their &quot;always on&quot; radar.<br /> <br /> In fact, Obi-wan is a pretty good example of how this might play out in Mage... His Perception + Awareness is high enough to feel a small moon sized light saber blow up a planet. He doesn't have to actively use the Force to monitor the universe for exploding planets. Then, he either actively used Awareness, probably Intelligence + Awareness based on the description of Perception as &quot;notice and Intelligence as &quot;analyze&quot;, get the &quot;as if a thousand voices cried out and were silenced&quot; bit. (He must have gotten a lot of successes, since that was 100% accurate.) That seems like it fits under Awareness as described. Alternatively, he could have used some kind of effect (Prime? Life?) to analyze the &quot;blip&quot;. I guess you could require MASSIVE amounts of Correspondence or just say the &quot;wavefront&quot; of death hit HIM not so much as he subconsciously reached out to it. So it was effectively a localized effect. It would take Correspondence to find out WHERE the the 1000's of voices were silenced. <br /> <br /> Meaning, I would probably say that a vamp using Clairvoyance would potentially trip a mage's Perception + Awareness reflexively. Probably not easily. A lot of those kind of roles seem to be set as Diff. 8 in the rules. Then the mage could quickly do a &quot;from the hip&quot; analysis using Intelligence + Awareness to get a vague idea of what is going on. (&quot;I feel a presence in this room. It is watching us.&quot;) And/or the mage could start using Foci to put up effects that would get real info. (Correspodence would pinpoint the origin of the effect. Mind and or Prime to sense the effect and its nature. Etc. It's Mage. Mix and match to your heart's content.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T13:22:17-08:00","id":1028668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Based on the description of Awareness (and Alertness) and of Perception in the core book, they can be used actively or reflexively. </div> </div> </div>Yes, you're right. I missinterpreted a line in Revised (in the Awareness skill) that says that &quot;A mage can use Awareness if he suspects something is mystical...however sometimes the Storyteller rolls to see if the mage senses something wierd that isn't eviden&quot;. I tought that the ST intervention was only sometimes, but reading it in the light of your comment, it means that &quot;when something magical isn't evident, the Storytellers rolls Awareness to see if the mage notices&quot;. Thanks for the data.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T13:44:58-08:00","id":1028673,"title":"","content":"You would definitely need Mind to analyse the projection, as it is not spiritual in nature, and it would be difficult to track it to its source. It is also a high level power and, at least in the earlier crossover rules, you have to have equivalent or higher level powers to interact with it. Since it is a level five power, that would mean Mind 5 to analyse, Correspondence 5 to track, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T23:54:45-08:00","id":1028904,"title":"","content":"Vampire breaks that rule by itself.<br /> If a vampire peeks at another leech who happens to have Auspex(active), and he rolls a success using Auspex as a pool, then he gets a hint/feeling/whatever.<br /> This is true if you only have Auspex 1.<br /> <br /> My Crossover Policy: <br /> 1. Don't do Crossover! <br /> 2. If you must, then choose one splat's corebook to have precedence over the rest.<br /> 3. Don't use the Crossover Rules.<br /> 4. If you insist, then don't complain if you encounter any problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}